=== COMP_WORDBREAKS
$' \t\n"\'><=;|&('
=== COMP_WORDS is cut at the break characters, runs of them kept whole
CWORD=3 WORDS=<cmd><--opt><=><va> cur=<va> prev=<=> TYPE=64 KEY=9
[cmd --opt=va][]
CWORD=2 WORDS=<cmd><--opt><=> cur=<> prev=<--opt> TYPE=64 KEY=9
[cmd --opt=][]
CWORD=4 WORDS=<cmd><a><>>><b><c> cur=<c> prev=<b> TYPE=64 KEY=9
[cmd a>>b c][]
CWORD=2 WORDS=<cmd><"x=y"><z> cur=<z> prev=<"x=y"> TYPE=64 KEY=9
[cmd "x=y" z][]
CWORD=4 WORDS=<cmd><2><>&><1><a> cur=<a> prev=<1> TYPE=64 KEY=9
[cmd 2>&1 a][]
=== without = in COMP_WORDBREAKS the word stays whole
CWORD=1 WORDS=<cmd><--opt=va> cur=<--opt=va> prev=<cmd> TYPE=64 KEY=9
[cmd --opt=va][]
[cmd --opt=value ][]
=== a reply goes in after the last break character
[cmd --opt=value ][]
=== COMP_TYPE: TAB-like, listing, menu, insert
CWORD=1 WORDS=<cmd><x> cur=<x> prev=<cmd> TYPE=9 KEY=9
[cmd x][]
CWORD=1 WORDS=<cmd><x> cur=<x> prev=<cmd> TYPE=63 KEY=63
[cmd x][]
CWORD=1 WORDS=<cmd><x> cur=<x> prev=<cmd> TYPE=42 KEY=42
[cmd x][]
CWORD=1 WORDS=<cmd><x> cur=<x> prev=<cmd> TYPE=37 KEY=109
[cmd x][]
=== compopt changes the running completion
[c1 word][]
[c2 with\ space ][]
[c3 with space ][]
compopt +o bashdefault +o default +o dirnames +o filenames +o noquote +o nosort -o nospace +o plusdirs
[c4 x][]
=== -o options
[o1 with\ space ][]
dir1/  dir2/\r\n
dir1/  dir2/  dzz\r\n
[o4 with\ space ][]
zeta   alpha  mid\r\n
=== a -D loader that returns 124 has the real spec used
[lazy loaded-word ][]
complete -F lazy_complete lazy
[other lo][]
